fastVEP fixtures: a 50-variant slice of chromosome 22 (GRCh38, Ensembl 116).

Variants: rows of the platform-2610-2 variant index
(gs://open-targets-pipeline-runs/do/platform-2610-2/output/variant), chromosome 22,
positions 19,700,000-20,100,000, plus 22_18521430_A_G, which is intergenic only here
because the GFF3 is cut. chr22_slice_rows.parquet holds them (chromosome, position, rsId,
referenceAllele, alternateAllele), sorted by position and alleles; chr22_slice.vcf is pts
write_vcf(rows, path, sequence) of them, whose ID is the row's 0-based ordinal. fastVEP
echoes it as each JSON record's top-level "id".

chr22_slice.gff3.gz: Homo_sapiens.GRCh38.116.chromosome.22.gff3.gz from the Ensembl FTP,
cut to the 88 genes overlapping 19,200,000-20,600,000 and their descendants, then put
through pts prepare_gff3 (3 readthrough transcripts dropped).

chr22_slice.fa.gz: contig 22, full length (50,818,468), all N except the Ensembl REST
release 116 bases of 22:19700000-20080000 and 22:18521330-18521530.

../fastvep_sample.json: fastVEP v0.4.0 (Huang-lab/fastVEP release, aarch64-apple-darwin;
the x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu binary writes the same bytes) on the uncompressed GFF3 and
FASTA, through pts build_cache then run_fastvep with 2 threads, i.e.

  fastvep cache --gff3 chr22_slice.gff3 --no-progress -o CACHE
  fastvep annotate --input EMPTY.vcf --fasta chr22_slice.fa --transcript-cache CACHE FLAGS -o EMPTY.json
  RAYON_NUM_THREADS=2 fastvep annotate --input chr22_slice.vcf --fasta chr22_slice.fa \
    --transcript-cache CACHE FLAGS -o fastvep_sample.json

  FLAGS = --pick-allele-gene --pick-order mane_select,canonical --distance 500000
          --symbol --hgvs --canonical --output-format json --no-progress

Check with FASTVEP_BINARY=<fastvep>: test_run_fastvep_chr22_slice compares
its output with fastvep_sample.json.

chr22_slice_transcripts.parquet: transcript_fields-shaped rows (Ensembl 116) for the 866
transcripts of chr22_slice.gff3.gz. Coordinates, strand, biotype and canonical come from the
GFF3; APPRIS (written back in the core form, e.g. principal1), MANE, UniProt accessions (all
in swissprot) and symbols from the platform-2610-2 transcriptConsequences of the 50 variants,
null where that index has none; mature_mirna is ENST00000585066's core-table pair,
19963755-19963775 and 19963814-19963834.
